      ms: 2760
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Don''t: building now means a loss.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2920
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||It foresees the squeeze: minus two if it builds, zero if it doesn''t. The mould is never made.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6440
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||And both lose. Ten thousand dollars of gains vanish, because a promise can''t be trusted.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6920
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:o8go6g'
    '|b||Once the mould could fetch what it cost somewhere else, the squeeze stops hurting, and it gets built. Specificity is what gives the threat its bite.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8600
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||So a specific investment invites hold-up, and the fear of hold-up kills good investments. Williamson''s cure: the more specific the asset, the less you leave to the market.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12520
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Standard parts, like bolts: just buy them. Something tailor-made: sign a long contract. Something no one else could use: make it yourself.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8600
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1b1xkag'
    '|a||Inside one firm, there''s no one left to squeeze. The mould shop and the yard share one bottom line.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:nihc71'
    '|b||In 1978 Benjamin Klein, Robert Crawford and Armen Alchian told GM and Fisher this way.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7400
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1k5rn8p'
    '|a||Car demand boomed in the mid-1920s, and GM wanted Fisher to build a body plant beside its own plant in Flint.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1auqdnt'
    '|b||Fisher refused. Under cost plus, a costly, out-of-the-way set-up paid more, since the seventeen point six percent rode on every extra dollar.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9160
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1g2ezku'
    '|a||This time the supplier did the squeezing: GM was tied by its exclusive contract. So in 1926 it made instead of bought.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:hebodv'
    '|b||One story proves little. Paul Joskow looked at 277 contracts between coal mines and power plants.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7680
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:55rxre'
    '|a||Plants built right at the mouth of a mine, with nowhere else to buy, signed much longer contracts. Just what the theory predicts.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:836nno'
    '|b||Sanford Grossman, Oliver Hart and John Moore added a twist: owning means deciding whatever no contract foresaw. So give ownership to the side whose investment matters most.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12320
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1lfnw1'
    '|a||There''s a one-line rule behind the hold-up game. Show the math, or skip it?':
